        "source": "import triton\nimport triton.language as tl\n\n@triton.jit\ndef layernorm_stats(X, S, N: tl.constexpr, BLOCK: tl.constexpr):\n    row = tl.program_id(0)\n    col = tl.arange(0, BLOCK)\n    mask = col < N\n    x = tl.load(X + row * N + col, mask, other=0.0)\n    mean = tl.sum(x, 0) / N\n    centered = tl.where(mask, x - mean, 0.0)\n    var = tl.sum(centered * centered, 0) / N\n    inv = tl.rsqrt(var + 1e-5)\n    tl.store(S + 2 * row, mean)\n    tl.store(S + 2 * row + 1, inv)\n\n@triton.jit\ndef layernorm_apply(X, W, B, S, Y, TOTAL: tl.constexpr, N: tl.constexpr, BLOCK: tl.constexpr):\n    program_idx = tl.program_id(0)\n    offs = tl.arange(0, BLOCK)\n    i = program_idx * BLOCK + offs\n    mask = i < TOTAL\n    row = i // N\n    col = i % N\n    x = tl.load(X + i, mask, other=0.0)\n    mean = tl.load(S + 2 * row, mask, other=0.0)\n    inv = tl.load(S + 2 * row + 1, mask, other=0.0)\n    w = tl.load(W + col, mask, other=0.0)\n    b = tl.load(B + col, mask, other=0.0)\n    val = (x - mean) * inv * w + b\n    tl.store(Y + i, val, mask)\n",
        "rationale": "Refined index computation in layernorm_apply for clarity and correctness by explicitly assigning program_id and offsets to variables before computing linear indices. This avoids potential indexing mistakes and ensures consistent masking for load/store operations at irregular tensor boundaries. The rest of the code maintains the previously improved BLOCK=256 tiling and explicit masking to handle irregular dimension sizes safely and efficiently, preserving correctness and improving memory access coalescing."
